## 30. Statements to avoid

Avoid:

> S3 is the complete historical genetic base.

Use:

> S3 was the broadest pre-1973 historical set identifiable from animals with recorded birth years in the available pedigree.

Avoid:

> Truncating the pedigree creates incorrect founders.

Use:

> Truncating the pedigree changes the pedigree base and removes ancestral relationships outside the retained pedigree.

Avoid:

> Marginal contribution is better than all other pedigree methods.

Use:

> Marginal ancestor contribution was selected because the study question concerned retained historical influence while accounting for overlapping pedigree pathways.

Avoid:

> Every unmatched historical animal contributed nothing.

Use:

> Unmatched historical animals did not appear as separate marginal contributors in the returned ancestor table for that reference population.

Avoid:

> Studbook closure caused the historical contribution to change.

Use:

> Historical contribution was compared across reference populations defined relative to the 1998 studbook-closure breakpoint; causal interpretation requires additional evidence.

